{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And Amalek came.</b> One wonders why he delayed fighting with Israel until now and did not come immediately when they went down to Egypt, when they were only seventy souls. One may say that the Holy One, blessed be He, said to Abraham: ״ועבדום וענו אותם״. And when our father Abraham, of blessed memory, died, the obligation fell upon Isaac. And when Isaac died, it fell upon Jacob and his sons, and upon Esau and his sons. And Amalek the wicked said in his heart: if I destroy Jacob and his seed, the obligation will fall upon me. Therefore he waited until they came out of Egypt, by which time the obligation had already been exacted, and then he came to fight with them."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:03:17.595653969Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}